Q: Difference between single quotes and double quotes in SQL A: <p>Double quotes are for names of tables or fields. Sometimes you can omit them. The single quotes are for string constants. This is the SQL standard. In the verbose form, your query looks like this:</p>
<pre><code>select *
from &quot;employee&quot;
where &quot;employee_name&quot; = 'elina';
</code></pre>
